sentences.l:
—“Let-us-ask-for our wives from-the Çid Campeador,
let-us-say that them we-will-take to lands of Carrión,
show them we-will where [th]ey endow[e]d are.

sentences.t:
Sacar las hemos de Valençia, de poder del Campeador;
después en la carrera feremos nuestro sabor,
ante que nos retrayan lo que cuntió del león.

sentences.l:
Take-out them we-will from Valençia, from power of-the Campeador;
afterwards on the road we-will-do our pleasure,
before that us they-cast-up what befell of-the lion.

sentences.t:
Nos de natura somos de co[m]des de Carrión!
Averes levaremos grandes que valen grant valor;
escarniremos las fijas del Canpeador.”

sentences.l:
We by birth are of counts of Carrión!
Goods we-will-carry great that are-worth great value;
we-will-shame the daughters of-the Campeador.”

sentences.t:
darvos e mulas e palafrés, muy gruessos de sazón
cavallos pora en diestro fuertes e corredores,
e muchas vestiduras de paños e de çiclatones;

sentences.l:
give-you I-will mules and palfreys, very stout of season
horses for at-right-hand strong and swift,
and many garments of cloths and of silks;

sentences.t:
Atorgado lo han esto iffantes de Carrión.
Aquí reçiben fijas del Campeador;
conpieçan a reçebir lo que el Çid mandó.

sentences.l:
Granted it have this Infantes of Carrión.
Here they-receive daughters of-the Campeador;
they-begin to receive what the Çid gave.

sentences.t:
“Merçed vos pedimos, padre, sí vos vala el Criador!
vos nos engendrastes, nuestra madre nos parió;
delant sodes amos, señora e señor.

sentences.l:
“Grace from-you we-ask, father, so you may-help the Creator!
you us begot, our mother us bore;
before us you-are both, lady and lord.

sentences.t:
El[l]e fizo aquesto, la madre lo doblava;
“Andad, fijas; d' aquí el Criador vos vala!
de mí e de vuestro padre, bien avedes nuestra graçia.

sentences.l:
He did this, the mother it was-doubling;
“Go, daughters; from here the Creator you may-help!
from me and from your father, well you-have our favour.
